{"parentUuid":"5c3b3ca7-cc8a-430b-bfdd-142cbf4f26d7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a6953ba7-830f-4ac5-9194-491b45e02392","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KQBpvBeRrZLCQFEhfHrv8v","type":"tool_result","content":"14\t\n15\t/// Content fingerprint of a fetched page, used as a pagination loop guard: a\n16\t/// server that ignores the page/offset parameter (or clamps to the last page)\n17\t/// returns the same non-empty page on every request, which would otherwise loop\n18\t/// forever. Stopping when two consecutive pages fingerprint identically mirrors\n19\t/// Substitute `${name}` tokens with flow-captured login values (#567) — e.g. an\n20\t/// Intacct `sessionid` captured from the login response and needed inside every\n21\t/// data request's raw XML body. Only exact `${name}` occurrences for a captured\n22\t/// `name` are replaced; any other `${...}` token is left untouched. Applied per\n23\t/// request, after the parent-context substitution.\n24\tfn substitute_captured(s: &str, captured: &BTreeMap<String, String>) -> String {\n25\t    if captured.is_empty() || !s.contains(\"${\") {\n26\t        return s.to_string();\n27\t    }\n28\t    let mut out = s.to_string();\n29\t    for (k, v) in captured {\n30\t        out = out.replace(&format!(\"${{{k}}}\"), v);\n31\t    }\n32\t    out\n33\t}\n34\t\n35\t/// the REST source's body-fingerprint guard (audit #146 H4/H5).\n36\tfn page_fingerprint(records: &[Value]) -> u64 {\n37\t    use std::hash::{Hash, Hasher};\n38\t    // `serde_json::Value` is not `Hash`; hash its canonical string form.\n39\t    let mut hasher = std::collections::hash_map::DefaultHasher::new();\n40\t    records.len().hash(&mut hasher);\n41\t    for r in records {\n42\t        r.to_string().hash(&mut hasher);\n43\t    }\n44\t    hasher.finish()\n45\t}\n46\t"}]},"uuid":"57920eae-8af3-4091-ae57-1a0e48cf43dd","timestamp":"2026-08-24T04:43:19.455Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream/crates/source/xml/src/stream.rs","content":"\n/// Content fingerprint of a fetched page, used as a pagination loop guard: a\n/// server that ignores the page/offset parameter (or clamps to the last page)\n/// returns the same non-empty page on every request, which would otherwise loop\n/// forever. Stopping when two consecutive pages fingerprint identically mirrors\n/// Substitute `${name}` tokens with flow-captured login values (#567) — e.g. an\n/// Intacct `sessionid` captured from the login response and needed inside every\n/// data request's raw XML body. Only exact `${name}` occurrences for a captured\n/// `name` are replaced; any other `${...}` token is left untouched. Applied per\n/// request, after the parent-context substitution.\nfn substitute_captured(s: &str, captured: &BTreeMap<String, String>) -> String {\n    if captured.is_empty() || !s.contains(\"${\") {\n        return s.to_string();\n    }\n    let mut out = s.to_string();\n    for (k, v) in captured {\n        out = out.replace(&format!(\"${{{k}}}\"), v);\n    }\n    out\n}\n\n/// the REST source's body-fingerprint guard (audit #146 H4/H5).\nfn page_fingerprint(records: &[Value]) -> u64 {\n    use std::hash::{Hash, Hasher};\n    // `serde_json::Value` is not `Hash`; hash its canonical string form.\n    let mut hasher = std::collections::hash_map::DefaultHasher::new();\n    records.len().hash(&mut hasher);\n    for r in records {\n        r.to_string().hash(&mut hasher);\n    }\n    hasher.finish()\n}\n","numLines":33,"startLine":14,"totalLines":1127}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5c3b3ca7-cc8a-430b-bfdd-142cbf4f26d7","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"feat/bigquery-auto-create-table","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
